 "description": "Four ranges – the Purcells, Selkirks, Monashees and Cariboos – forming the first major mountain barrier east of the Coast Mountains in southern and east-central BC. Deep snowpacks, glaciers and an interior temperate rainforest characterise Glacier and Mount Revelstoke national parks. Kootenay lake and river valleys (Nelson, Castlegar, Revelstoke) lie between the ranges.",
